The three defect terminals are `StabilizedSurvivor`, `OpenObstruction`, and `ExactRepair`. Their canonical aggregate is `StabilizedSurvivor`, with both residuals retained.

## Aggregation policy

Dominance order is `InfrastructureFailure > Invalid > Refused > OracleNeeded > LiftLicenseNeeded > trichotomy`. Within the trichotomy, all exact repairs yield `ExactRepair`; open-only evidence yields `OpenObstruction`; stabilized evidence yields `StabilizedSurvivor`; and exact progress plus an open survivor yields `StabilizedSurvivor`. This follows the existing bounded partial-repair semantics while the residual ledger keeps every open local claim visible.

| Truth row | Local terminals | Expected aggregate |
|---|---|---|
| exact-only | ExactRepair | ExactRepair |
| stabilized-only | StabilizedSurvivor | StabilizedSurvivor |
| open-only | OpenObstruction | OpenObstruction |
| partial-repair-open | ExactRepair, OpenObstruction | StabilizedSurvivor |
| stabilized-plus-open | StabilizedSurvivor, OpenObstruction | OpenObstruction |
| partial-repair-mixed-survivors | ExactRepair, StabilizedSurvivor, OpenObstruction | StabilizedSurvivor |
| lift-dominates-trichotomy | ExactRepair, LiftLicenseNeeded | LiftLicenseNeeded |
| oracle-dominates-lift | LiftLicenseNeeded, OracleNeeded | OracleNeeded |
| refusal-dominates-oracle | OracleNeeded, Refused | Refused |
| invalid-dominates-refusal | Refused, Invalid | Invalid |
| infrastructure-dominates-invalid | Invalid, InfrastructureFailure | InfrastructureFailure |

The hostile suite additionally enumerates all 512 triples over the eight-terminal vocabulary and all six permutations of each triple. Every permutation produces the same aggregate.

