## Surviving obstructions

- This is one frozen three-defect, six-subclaim matrix, not unrestricted GTOC-6 over arbitrary carriers, defect families, diagnostic rules, or predecessor receipts.
- The bounded GTOC-3 predecessor did not issue a lift license. The S06-002 lift residual is preserved, not repaired or hidden.
- S14-005/GTOC-5 remains absent and `NOT_EVALUATED`; the named proof-obligation residual does not complete or authorize it.
- S06-004/GTOC-8 still requires its own import/oracle packet and the separately constructed GTOC-7 migration receipt. It may consume only this bounded S06-003 evidence.
- The verifier is a library and fixture suite, not a signed binary, activated runtime gate, protected-branch policy, host lease controller, or mutation enforcer.
- SAGA-14 still owns certificate-to-authority enforcement and any future `AuthorizedLocalResult` constructor.

## Nonclaims

This sprint does not establish GTOC-5, unrestricted GTOC-6, GTOC-7, or GTOC-8; cover arbitrary defects, dynamic rules, imports, carrier families, or every repository receipt; issue or execute a lift license; prove a general cochain theorem; run a live model; activate a gate; sign a binary; mutate a protected branch; authenticate a human; record human promotion; mint authority; create `AuthorizedLocalResult`; instantiate an autonomous successor; or run Lean.
